1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
A coding agent can pass tests without fixing the bug:

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:10,000
edit the tests, hardcode values, or forge the report.

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:15,000
ProofLoop is an independent acceptance layer for untrusted code.

4
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:21,000
The agent edits code inside a Docker sandbox on Vultr.

5
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:27,000
The control plane holds the Vultr key; it never enters the sandbox.

6
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:33,000
The containment probe starts a fresh container.

7
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:38,000
It tries the network — blocked.

8
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:43,000
Secret-looking environment variables — none visible.

9
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:49,000
512 megabytes, one CPU, all capabilities dropped.

10
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:55,000
Now a real Vultr Serverless Inference agent fixes the bug.

11
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:01,000
Every tool call is a fresh container with no network and no key.

12
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:07,000
ProofLoop re-runs the patch under its own sandbox.

13
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:13,000
Fourteen deterministic checks, hidden tests, mutation, coverage.

14
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:19,000
Scene one passes: fourteen of fourteen checks.

15
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:25,000
The evidence sheet is hash-addressed and replayable.

16
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:31,000
Same verifier, cheat patch: the hidden test fails.

17
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:37,000
The hardcoded lookup table is flagged by name.

18
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:43,000
Verify the evidence hash and replay the run.

19
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:50,000
Trust the evidence, not the agent.
